-- ============================================================================
-- PG-OMITTED-BY-DESIGN: the CodeGen metadata-refresh EXECUTE block
--
-- The SS original ends with six calls — spUpdateExistingEntitiesFromSchema,
-- spUpdateSchemaInfoFromDatabase, spDeleteUnneededEntityFields,
-- spUpdateExistingEntityFieldsFromSchema, spSetDefaultColumnWidthWhereNeeded and
-- spRecompileAllProceduresInDependencyOrder. They are deliberately absent here, not lost.
--
-- On PostgreSQL those routines are maintained in TypeScript
-- (packages/CodeGenLib/src/Database/providers/postgresql/metadataSupportObjects.ts), and the work
-- the block performs is already done here by two other means: the inlined R__RefreshMetadata copy
-- above reconciles the EntityField rows and sequences, and `convert --bake-codegen` bakes the
-- generated objects into this migration. Re-running the SS block would be redundant, and
-- spRecompileAllProceduresInDependencyOrder has no PG meaning at all — PL/pgSQL plans are
-- per-session, so there is nothing to recompile. This matches every committed counterpart whose SS
-- original carried the same block (10 of them across v5).
--
-- Stated explicitly because an omission that is correct is indistinguishable, on inspection, from
-- the silent-emptying defect that shipped in v5.45 (issue #3253).
-- ============================================================================
